  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Preheat oven to 240°C/220°C fan-forced. To a medium bowl, add haloumi and cover with water to soak.\n• Place sweet potato fries on a lined oven tray. Drizzle with olive oil, sprinkle over All-American spice blend and season with salt.\n• Bake until tender, 20-25 minutes. TIP: If your oven tray is crowded, divide between two trays.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-6507c73f264c5c170b2da4e1-0b702d4e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, slice apple (see ingredients) into thin sticks.\n• When fries have 10 minutes remaining, in a shallow bowl, place the plain flour. In a second shallow bowl, whisk the egg. In a third shallow bowl, place panko breadcrumbs.\n• Drain haloumi and pat dry then slice in half to get 2 pieces per person.\n• Dip haloumi slices into flour mixture, then into egg and finally in panko breadcrumbs. Set aside on a plate. TIP: Press the haloumi firmly into the flour mixture to help it stick!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-6507c73f264c5c170b2da4e1-0ff33488.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a medium frying pan, heat enough olive oil to coat the base over medium-high heat.\n• When oil is hot, cook haloumi until golden brown, 2 minutes each side.\n• Transfer to a paper towel-lined plate.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-6507c73f264c5c170b2da4e1-80334f71.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• While haloumi is cooking, in a large bowl, combine apple, slaw mix, ranch dressing and a drizzle of olive oil and white wine vinegar. Season.\n• Divide American crumbed haloumi, sweet potato fries and apple slaw between plates.\n• Serve with dill & parsley mayonnaise. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-6507c73f264c5c170b2da4e1-e436ec60.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
